{{- define "review_handoff" -}}
## Handoff to the User

{{ .GateLabel }} stopped its automatic loop: {{ .Reason }}

Before any other work, ask the user exactly one question with the ask-user tool described under Asking Questions. Use this question text verbatim:

> {{ blockquote .Question }}

Offer exactly these options, with these labels:
- "{{ .ContinueLabel }}": the user types guidance as the answer; you apply it and {{ .GateLabel }} continues.
- "{{ .AcceptLabel }}": the open findings are accepted as they are and {{ .AcceptOutcome }}.
- "{{ .StopLabel }}": {{ .GateLabel }} stops; the user resumes or rewinds the feature later.

If the answer is "{{ .AcceptLabel }}" or "{{ .StopLabel }}", make no changes and finish. Any other answer is the user's guidance: apply it as this round's fix, using the open findings as reviewer feedback where the guidance leaves something open, then finish. The harness records the answer in the decisions file.

Open findings and the previous fixer's note: {{ .NotePath }}

